# CODEOWNERS — DSX AI Factory community repository
#
# Every pull request requires review from the owners of the paths it touches.
# This is the enforcement mechanism for the content approval process described
# in the POR governance model.
#
# STATUS: the teams below DO NOT EXIST YET. They must be created by a
# dsx-ai-factory organization owner before this file has any effect — GitHub
# silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries that name a non-existent team. Until the
# teams exist, this file documents the intended ownership model rather than
# enforcing it. See GOVERNANCE.md for the team-request list.
#
# Role mapping to the POR staffing table:
#   dsx-community-editors     -> Editor (overall PIC, roadmap and content)
#   dsx-community-maintainers -> Maintainer (CI/CD, review/approve/merge/publish)
#   dsx-community-product     -> Product delegates (one per component team)
#   dsx-community-partners    -> Partner delegates (one per partner program area)
#   dsx-community-moderators  -> Community Representative (discussion moderation)

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                           @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors

# Published articles. Editors own the content; maintainers own the publish path.
/content/                   @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors
/content/posts/             @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors

# Articles that showcase a partner or customer additionally require a partner
# delegate, who confirms the mention is cleared with that partner.
/content/posts/partners/    @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-partners

# Articles centred on a specific component additionally require that component's
# product delegate. Add per-component paths here as components are onboarded.
/content/posts/components/  @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-product

# Site build, publishing pipeline, and automation.
/.github/                   @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/site/                      @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers

# Compliance and governance files. Changing any of these can invalidate the
# repository's Open Source Review Board approval, so they carry the tightest
# ownership.
/LICENSE                    @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md     @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-moderators @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md              @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-editors @dsx-ai-factory/dsx-community-maintainers
